    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10329" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjectātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		conjecto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a conjecturing, guessing, conjecture, surmise</i>
			(post-Aug.; mostly in Plin. the elder; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Quint.): ingens opum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 19, 22, § 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plana de deo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2,
					7, 5, § 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obscura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 75, 97, § 209</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lubrica atque ambagiosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 14, 1, 33</span></i>
			.</div>
